---
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";

const stats = [
  { value: "~5", label: "Years experience" },
  { value: "5", label: "B2B/B2C products" },
  { value: "1K+", label: "Monthly users" },
  { value: "60%", label: "Faster loads" },
  { value: "15", label: "LMS routes audited" },
  { value: "~30%", label: "AI productivity" },
];
---

<section id="about" class="scroll-mt-16" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <SectionHeading
    id="about"
    index="01"
    eyebrow="About"
    title="What I do, and the numbers behind it"
    lead="Nearly five years of frontend work in education and travel tech, the last two leading a team. In short: I build the web side of large products, make them faster, and set the standards the other engineers work to."
  />

  <p class="mb-8 max-w-[68ch]">
    Hi there! I&apos;m Hà. I lead frontend at SAPP Academy, where I own the
    architecture of a learning platform students and teachers use every day —
    the technical direction, the coding standards, the code reviews, and two
    junior engineers. Before that, five B2B/B2C products at a travel group,
    working both the React frontend and the Spring Boot services behind it.
    React, Next.js and TypeScript are the day-to-day; architecture, performance
    and developer experience are the part I&apos;m actually hired for.
  </p>

  <ul class="mb-10 grid grid-cols-2 border-t-2 border-l-2 border-rule sm:grid-cols-3">
    {
      stats.map((stat) => (
        <li class="border-r-2 border-b-2 border-rule px-4 py-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold tabular-nums text-ink">
            {stat.value}
          </p>
          <p class="label mt-1 text-ink-3">{stat.label}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <div class="border-l-4 border-ink pl-5">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg">Frontend Tech Lead · SAPP Academy</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2.5">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>Led frontend architecture across the product ecosystem.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Built a <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Monorepo</strong> with
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">pnpm Workspace</strong> and
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Turborepo</strong>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Migrated the LMS from
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">
              Next.js 12 → Next.js 14 (App Router)
            </strong>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Ran a performance pass across 15 LMS routes — took <code>/courses</code>
            from <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">15.2s → 6.1s</strong> with
            Lighthouse Performance <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">29 → 65</strong>,
            lifting the student route group to
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">49 → 67</strong> —
            <a class="link" href="#performance">the audit, and the fix I held back</a>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Replaced a
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">per-seat TinyMCE licence</strong>
            with a custom <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Tiptap</strong>
            package across the monorepo. The editor sits in front of every student
            and teacher, so the bill tracked enrolment — the one number nobody can
            forecast a year out, and an unforecastable seat count is an
            unbudgetable line item.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="border-l-4 border-ink pl-5">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg">Full-stack Developer · Tweet World Travel Group</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2.5">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Developed Spring Boot microservices and high-performance React /
            Next.js applications.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Delivered <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">5 B2B/B2C products</strong>
            serving approximately
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">1,000 monthly users</strong>.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="border-l-4 border-ink pl-5">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg">Additional highlights</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2.5">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Integrated security CI/CD with Gitleaks, Trivy, Semgrep, and ZAP —
            gating <a class="link" href="#performance">every merge request</a>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            Designed AI workflows that improved engineering productivity by
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink"> ~30%</strong>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            B.Eng in Electronics &amp; Telecommunications (HUST) · Published
            research at <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">REV-ECIT 2021</strong>.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
